blocks.en:
The finding of § 5 remains a paradox in a single-task setting: why distill when you already have the GRPO-trained model? Across multiple tasks, however, the paradox can become an opportunity. Consider math and code: separate GRPO runs produce two specialists, but
neither checkpoint can serve both domains (Appendix F ). This is where multi-teacher OPD has a distinct compute-efficiency opportunity: it can consolidate the GRPO specialists into a single multi-domain model that neither specialist provides, with only a small additional distillation cost. This opportunity only exists when the answer to the following question is true: Would the cost of training those experts and consolidating them via distillation beat that of joint GRPO on the same data mix? Recent open-source models ( Yang et al., 2026d ; Team et al., 2026 ; DeepSeek-AI, 2026 ; Kimi Team, 2026 ) use this recipe;
we set out to understand the rationale behind it.

blocks.zh:
§5的发现在单一任务环境下仍然是自相矛盾的:为什么在已经有GPRO训练的模型时会蒸馏? 然而,在多重任务中,悖论可能成为一个机会。 考虑数学和代码: 单独的GPRO运行 产生两个专家,但
两个检查点都无法为两个域服务(附录F )。 这正是多教师OPD具有独特的计算效率机会的地方:它可以将GPRO专家整合为一个单一的多领域模型,而两者都不是专家提供的,只有少量的额外蒸馏成本. 只有当对下列问题的回答属实时,才存在这一机会: 培训这些专家以及通过蒸馏整合这些专家的费用是否将比联合GPRO在同一数据组合上的费用高? 最近的开源模型(杨等,2026d; Team等,2026;DeepSeek-AI,2026;Kimi Team,2026)使用此食谱;
我们开始理解它背后的理由。
